# ============================================================
# Cross-machine consistency policy (machineB)
# TRACK : only .py / .md / .txt  (scripts + docs + text), repo-wide.
# IGNORE: everything else — all binaries (png/jpg/pdf/zip/pt/pth/npz/npy/csv/log),
#         data, json/yaml/sh, notebooks, caches — are auto-ignored by the `*` rule
#         below (they are simply not whitelisted). Plus the excluded dirs/files
#         re-listed at the bottom (results, dataset, temp, trash, references,
#         legacy, **/_deprecated, .claude, CLAUDE.md, ...).
# ============================================================

# 1) ignore everything, but keep descending into directories
*
!*/

# 2) whitelist scripts / docs / text only (+ keep .gitignore itself)
!*.py
!*.md
!*.txt
!.gitignore

# 3) re-exclude — these WIN over the whitelist above ==========

# -- excluded directory trees (no .py/.md/.txt tracked inside either) --
results/
comparison/results/
dataset/
temp/
.trash/
trash/
references/
ResearchProposal/
legacy/
**/_deprecated/
.claude/

# -- excluded specific files --
CLAUDE.md

# -- .py / .txt junk that must stay ignored despite the whitelist --
__pycache__/
*_backup*.py
*_option*.py
*.bak
*.backup
*.backup_*
*.py.bak
